  "notes": [
   "Units are quarter units; 'Major Required: 18-20 Credits' and 'Total Required: 18 - 20 Units' recorded as total_units 18-20.",
   "Page shows a 'Noncredit' tag but prints quarter units, not hours, so measure is units. Description says 'Pending state approval' while the footer says 'Program Status: Approved'.",
   "Catalog states cross-listed and honors versions earn credit for only one version, so cross-listed and honors pairs (e.g., AFAM 25/WMST 25, POLI 17/ICS 27/POLI 17H/ICS 27H) are recorded as one entry with alternatives.",
   "Catalog codes differ in format from the closed list but name the same courses: AFAM 12A=AFAM 012A, ARTS 2F=ARTS 002F, ASAM 30=ASAM030, E SD001.=E S 1 (and E SD002., E SD003., E SD004., E SD050.), ECONC2001=ECON C2001, POLSC1000=POLS C1000, HIST 7A=HIST 007A, ICS 2A=ICS 002A, and so on. 'E SD001.' etc. are kept exactly as printed.",
   "ICS 17, ICS 17H, ICS 19, POLI 15/ICS 25, POLI 16/ICS 36, POLI 17/ICS 27 (with honors) and WMST 1 appear in both the Intercultural Studies and Environmental Sustainability lists. It is not stated whether one course may satisfy both areas.",
   "In Intercultural Studies, ICS 2A and ICS 2B are 2 units each, so both would be needed to reach 4 units.",
   "Information Literacy (5 units) amounts to choosing one course (COMM 8/8H or PHIL 3).",
   "The outcomes list is the program's single list, recorded for this certificate."
  ]
